/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/docs/codex-testing-suite-design-6-21-26.md:607:2. A build run silently hung: status stayed RUNNING forever with the model idle and no UI error. Root cause: a sandbox file read raised SandboxError (a renamed file), which subclasses Exception (NOT the native OSError/FileNotFoundError hierarchy). ~8 call sites across the loop already had `except (FileNotFoundError, OSError, ...)` handlers intending to tolerate missing files — none catch SandboxError, so against the real sandbox backend they are all dead code; the exception escaped, killed the loop task, and nothing converted the crash into a terminal ERROR status.
